# Code Comments (tvscreener-rs)

- **Comments describe the code.** Explain what the code does (inputs, outputs, invariants), not marketing or process narrative.
- **Do not put app specs or marketing in code comments.** Put that in `docs/` - not in source.
- **Doc comments:** One line on what the function/type does in code terms.
- **Rust:** Use rustdoc `///` / `//!` on `pub` items. Prefer short `# Errors` / `# Panics` when Clippy requires them; keep them factual.
- Still obey `english-only.mdc` and the global no-em-dash rule.
